  m_Name: Scene13_FAQ_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene13_FAQ_1
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: 'It says the potential difference across a conductor equals the current through
    it multiplied by its resistance. Our nichrome wire: 5 ohms times 0.2 ampere gives
    1 volt, 5 ohms times 1 ampere gives 5 volts. Three clues, one relationship.'
  ttsText: 'It says the potential difference across a conductor equals the current
